{"name":"Lazulite","hex":"#003e65","fetched":"2026-10-28","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lazulite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A semi-precious gemstone that is a basic phosphate of magnesium, iron and aluminium"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lazulite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lazulite","blocks":[{"text":"Lazulite or Azure spar is a transparent to semi-opaque, blue mineral that is a phosphate of magnesium, iron, and aluminium, with the chemical formula (Mg,Fe2+)Al2(PO4)2(OH)2. Lazulite forms one endmember of a solid solution series with the darker, iron-rich scorzalite."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Lazulite-tmix07-168a.jpg/330px-Lazulite-tmix07-168a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lazulite","wikidata":"Q412651"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Lazulite-tmix07-168a.jpg/500px-Lazulite-tmix07-168a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Lazulite-tmix07-168a.jpg/500px-Lazulite-tmix07-168a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALazulite-tmix07-168a.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Lazulite-dtn2a.jpg/500px-Lazulite-dtn2a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Lazulite-dtn2a.jpg/500px-Lazulite-dtn2a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lazulite from Laila,(Village Dasso) Kutwal Valley Haramosh Gilgit District, Gilgit-Baltistan, Pakistan. Size: 2.4 cm × 1.7 cm × 0.8 cm (0.94 in × 0.67 in × 0.31 in).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALazulite-dtn2a.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Ba